  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an integer NNN.\n\nPrint a permutation PPP of [1,2,…,N][1,2, \\ldots, N][1,2,…,N] such that the following condition holds:\n\n\nFor any index i&nbsp;(1≤i&lt;N)i\\ (1 \\leq i \\lt N)i&nbsp;(1≤i&lt;N),  Pi×Pi+1P_i \\times P_{i+1}Pi​×Pi+1​ is not a perfect square.\nIf there are multiple correct answers, you may print **any** of them.\n\n**Note:** A permutation of [1,2,…,N][1, 2, \\ldots, N][1,2,…,N] is a rearrangement of those numbers.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN - the length of the required permutation.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print NNN space-separated integers representing the valid permutation on a single line.\n\n\nIf there are multiple correct answers, you may print **any** of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤5001 \\leq T \\leq 5001≤T≤500",
      "2≤N≤5002 \\leq N \\leq 5002≤N≤500"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n3\n4",
        "output": "2 1\n3 1 2\n4 2 3 1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: 2×1=22\\times 1 = 22×1=2 is not a perfect square. Note that [1,2][1, 2][1,2] is also a valid answer for this case, and will be accepted.\nTest case 222: 3×1=33\\times 1 = 33×1=3 and 1×2=21\\times 2 = 21×2=2 are not perfect squares.\nTest case 333: 4×2=8,2×3=6,3×1=34\\times 2 = 8, 2\\times 3 = 6, 3\\times 1 = 34×2=8,2×3=6,3×1=3 are all not perfect squares."
      }
    ]
  },
